The reliability doc predates the early-stop breaker and never said where the
gate can physically run. Both gaps cost real time: the gate needs a Docker
daemon, the app on CORE_LOOP_BASE_URL, and private credentials simultaneously,
and an environment missing the daemon cannot run it however complete the rest
of the configuration looks.

Adds two sections:

- Where to run it — the three simultaneous requirements, the wall-clock budget
  (50 attempts at up to 300s each), why a remote host needs tmux/screen, the
  smoke-before-gate sequence, and the npm ci / Rolldown-binding repair.
- When the campaign stops early — how to read earlyStop.signature, and the
  instruction not to rerun hoping for a better draw or raise the threshold.

The last paragraph is the one worth having in writing: if a campaign burned
many attempts on the same defect and the breaker never fired, the signatures
were not identical, which is a normalizer bug. The fix is a collapsing test
case in core-loop-report.test.ts, not a higher threshold.

